{"name":"Butterscotch","hex":"#fdb147","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"butterscotch","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard candy made from butter, brown sugar, syrup and vanilla.","A sauce or syrup made of similar ingredients."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light brown colour, like that of butterscotch candy.","Having the flavour of butterscotch."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/butterscotch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Butterscotch","blocks":[{"text":"Butterscotch is a type of confection whose primary ingredients are brown sugar and butter. Some recipes include cream, vanilla, and salt. The earliest known recipes, in mid-19th century Yorkshire, used treacle (molasses) in place of, or in addition to, sugar."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Butterscotch-Candies.jpg/330px-Butterscotch-Candies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butterscotch","wikidata":"Q2009326"},{"title":"Butterscotch (performer)","blocks":[{"text":"Antoinette Clinton, known professionally as Butterscotch, is an American beatboxer, singer, and musician."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Butterscotch_at_Montreux_Jazz_Festival.jpg/330px-Butterscotch_at_Montreux_Jazz_Festival.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butterscotch_(performer)","wikidata":"Q1018141"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Rye_%2815045370394%29.jpg/500px-Rye_%2815045370394%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Rye_%2815045370394%29.jpg/1280px-Rye_%2815045370394%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Rye_%281